----------------- Vertical Pod AutoScaling ------------------

Doc link for kubernetes auto-scaler :- https://github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler

Clone in your VM or EC2 instance :- 
. git clone https://github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler.git

After installation :-
1. cd in to the ./autoscaler/vertical-auto-scaler/ -->> Getting Started installation part

2. There u can see this thing and now follow step 3 :- 
git clone https://github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler.git
cd autoscaler/vertical-pod-autoscaler
git checkout origin/vpa-release-1.0
REGISTRY=registry.k8s.io/autoscaling TAG=1.0.0 ./hack/vpa-process-yamls.sh apply

3. Then run this ./hack/vpa-up.sh script file

----------------------------- VPA Mainfest ----------------------------

--> vim namespace.yml
-->
kind: Namespace
apiVersion: v1
metadata:
  name: apache


---> vim vpa.yml
--->
kind: VerticalPodAutoScaler
apiVersion: autoscaling.k8s.io/v1
metadata:
    name: apache-vpa
    namespace: apache

spec:
    targetRef:
        name: apache-deployment
        apiVersion: apps/v1
        kind: Deployment

        # Auto => Means based on the incoming requests, increase our pod resources vertically
        # Initial => Means initially u had assigned the resources so allocate them again  
    updatePolicy:
        updateMode: "Auto"  

. Then run the kubectl apply -f vpa.yml


. kubectl get vpa -n apache
. watch kubectl get vpa -n apache  // -->> for live actions

. kubectl top pod -n apache
. kubectl top node

